\quad\Longrightarrow\quad
\text{a complete finite exhaustion with proved tail bounds}.
\]

The phrase “relative to the certificate release” does not create a weaker mathematical notion of an odd perfect number. There are two different statements:

1. a finite collection of records is internally exhausted;
2. every hypothetical odd perfect number is represented by, and refuted within, that collection.

Only the second yields the advertised number-theoretic theorem.

The paper has not supplied a sufficient bridge between them.

