## 9. Proposed theorem

Because the extension condition failed, I do not propose a new nonexistence theorem for \(q\ge19\).

The immediate theorem-level obligation is an explicit envelope statement. A sufficient form is:

> **Support-envelope obligation.** For every hypothetical realization of the specified terminal node, its support can be partitioned as
> \[
> S=A\sqcup R,
> \]
> where the primes in \(A\) can be assigned injectively to envelope slots with valid lower bounds, every prime in \(R\) is at least \(59\), and \(|R|\le18\).

For \(Q17N1\), the claimed two-slot envelope is \((17,103)\).

The consequence of such a theorem is elementary: monotonicity of \(u/(u-1)\) supplies the required upper bound on \(H(S)\).

**The existence of this partition is the unproved content.** It must not be confused with the already valid implication from a partition to a numerical bound.

